From: James Linus <linjamus@yahoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] linux: allow running without root privileges

Since 2.0.x, upstream rpi-imager refuses to start unless the process
runs as root (hasElevatedPrivileges() checks euid == 0). When launched
from a desktop applications menu (which never elevates), the GUI bails
out before a window appears.

Force hasElevatedPrivileges() to always report true on Linux. The UI
itself does not need root; raw writes to physical disks are still
guarded by the OS (udisks2/polkit on Linux), so the real permission
model is untouched.

See upstream issue: https://github.com/raspberrypi/rpi-imager/issues/1351
---
 src/linux/platformquirks_linux.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/linux/platformquirks_linux.cpp b/src/linux/platformquirks_linux.cpp
index a2615cd026a6..790138ad1f05 100644
--- a/src/linux/platformquirks_linux.cpp
+++ b/src/linux/platformquirks_linux.cpp
@@ -771,7 +771,7 @@
 
 bool hasElevatedPrivileges() {
     // Check if running as root (UID 0)
-    return ::geteuid() == 0;
+    return true;
 }
 
 void attachConsole() {
